      "writtenOn": "2025-11-26T15:53:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just a quick question: since, as we agreed in aosp/3863270, we should always flush IOTLB in pKVM after unmap (and thus don\u0027t need to initiate flushing IOTLB from the host), do we still need to allow the host to submit any other QI descriptors than QI_IEC_TYPE (interrupt remapping)?\n\nIf not, maybe we shouldn\u0027t allow the host to submit any other descriptors?\n\nI.e. since we are not using nested translation for now, we can assume that IOTLB, context and PASID caches etc are fully \"owned\" by pKVM, and don\u0027t allow the host to meddle in their state, since the host has no reason to need to do that?",
      "revId": "68374c9efa17e512e5a65c5a8bd6c7d715b69fd3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3ab2f3f7_e0d5f5a8",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 70
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-26T16:00:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "interrupt remapping logic uses queued invalidation and is not handled by pkvm. So we might need to have this in host unless we move interrupt remapping support to pkvm. We could probably do some checks in pkvm not to allow any non interrupt entry cache invalidations?",
      "parentUuid": "b384c3a1_fa3b804c",
      "revId": "68374c9efa17e512e5a65c5a8bd6c7d715b69fd3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7336a50_7735a140",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 70
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-26T17:04:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, that\u0027s exactly my point. I understand we do need this hypercall since we do want the host to remain in charge of interrupt remapping. I\u0027m just wondering if the host needs this hypercall for any other types of QI invalidations (because it looks like it doesn\u0027t).\n\nSo if it doesn\u0027t, yeah, what I\u0027m suggesting is precisely to add some checks not to allow any non interrupt entry cache invalidations.\n\n(And if in the future we will use nested translation, I guess then we will also allow QI_EIOTLB_TYPE to let the host invalidate 1st-stage IOTLB.)",
      "parentUuid": "3ab2f3f7_e0d5f5a8",
      "revId": "68374c9efa17e512e5a65c5a8bd6c7d715b69fd3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
